<title>SPAIN: Spain's Santander studies San Paolo option.</title>
<headline>Spain's Santander studies San Paolo option.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Banco Santander said on Tuesday it was looking at an option to buy three percent of the share capital of Italy's Istituto Bancario San Paolo di Torino, but had not yet made a decision.</p>
<p>&quot;We are studying it,&quot; Santander chairman Emilio Botin told a news conference when asked about the option.</p>
<p>Santander already owns three percent of San Paolo. Italy's largest commercial bank is making a private share placement of around 20 percent of its stock to Italian and foreign investors in the next couple of months.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
